course: dictionary
lesson: 4320
title: Grove: a small wood or an orchard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grove is a small group of trees, or a small wood. The words around it give you clues. «A grove of aspens can be one giant plant, all trunks joined by one root system with the same genes.» Here the trees are a group that grows together, so grove means a small group of trees.
explain: Grove can also mean an orchard of fruit trees, such as an orange grove or an olive grove. When the sentence mentions oranges or olives, the word is probably this kind of grove. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try "small wood" or "orchard" in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: In stories, a grove is often a quiet, shady place, and sometimes a magical one. Words like shady and quiet help you picture it. Grove is also used in street names, like Elm Grove, so you may see it on a map.
fact: A grove is a small group of trees, or a small wood.
fact: «Grove» can also mean an orchard of fruit trees, such as an orange grove or olive grove.
fact: In stories, a grove is often quiet and shady, and sometimes magical.
fact: «A grove of aspens can be one giant plant»: Pando in Utah weighs about 6,000 tonnes.
fact: Grove is used in street names, as in Elm Grove.
exercise: «The children sheltered from the sun in the shady grove.» What is a grove here? | *A small wood | A stone wall | A river bank | A busy road
exercise: Mia says an orange grove is a pile of rocks. What is an orange grove? | *An orchard of orange trees | A shop that sells oranges | A hill covered in snow | A pile of rocks
exercise: «A grove of aspens can be one giant plant, all trunks joined by one root system.» Find and copy one word that means a small wood. | Utah | trunks | *grove | genes
test: «The olive grove glowed gold in the late sun.» What is an olive grove? | *An orchard of olive trees | A busy town square | A flock of birds | A rocky cliff by the sea
test: «The trunks of such a clone can all turn gold on the same autumn day.» Why can they all turn gold on the same day? | *They are all one plant with one root system | The autumn sun chose them on purpose | They are trees from different places that happened to meet | They were painted by the farmers
exam: In a story, the hero walked into a shady grove and sat down to rest. What is a grove? | A sandy beach by the sea | *A small wood, or a small group of trees | A fast-flowing river | A stone castle on a hill
